src/solweig_light and pyproject.toml are copied from:

  repository: https://github.com/Synn-Arch/SolweigLight2
  commit:     5a6dc4484211d658fbffb5c79b53187a404f8a2d  (2026-09-28, "Strip repository to runtime essentials")

with one local change, a Windows portability patch (no numerical change):

  - new src/solweig_light/_portable.py: file locks (fcntl on POSIX, msvcrt on
    Windows), directory fsync, read-only marking and file fsync per platform
  - persistence.py, cache/geometry.py, geometry/service.py,
    geometry/visibility_native.py and wind_resources.py call it instead of
    fcntl / os.open(directory) / os.chmod directly

Upstream imports fcntl unconditionally, which does not exist on Windows, so
students on Windows could not run the model at all. On POSIX the patched code
makes the same system calls as before. .github/workflows/model-platforms.yml
runs a small model run on Windows, macOS and Linux. Re-apply the patch (or merge
it upstream) when moving to a newer SolweigLight2 commit.

Both SolweigLight and SolweigLight2 report version 0.1.0.dev0, so this file is the
record of which source is in use. The Dockerfile import-checks a module that only
exists in SolweigLight2 (solweig_light.runtime_phases).
